s ventura so if it's  available on both ipad os and mac os the  new versions maybe apple wants to  release them at the same time which is  the reason for that delay which will be  in october and then going even deeper  stage manager is only available for m1  ipads which means that the new m2 ipad  pro that we're expecting in the fall is  also going to support stage manager so  what if that could be the release date  of the m2 ipad pro sometime in october  when apple says ipad os 16 should be  released alongside mac os ventura so  that's basically the biggest hint we  have of the m2 ipad pro coming at an  apple october event just like joe  resignal from mac rumors is saying we  could get the m2 ipad pro we could get  the new 10th gen ipad which i'm going to  talk about and ipad with 16 at the same  time however just like joe says right  here there is a chance that the 10gen  ipad could get a quick announcement  during the september event instead and  maybe it ships in september without the  new ipad with 16 or maybe they delay the  launch until october and release  everything at once i'm not sure but  that's also a possibility and now  getting into the actual design of the  next entry level 10 generation ipad we  had a major leak from my smart price  which actually has been correct in the  past showing off of course the new flat  sided redesign which is a huge deal now  getting into the actual renders right  here we can take a look and see some  huge differences first of all you have  the usbc port finally which means all of  apple's ipads will now be switching to  usb type-c which is a big deal and then  of course we have those flat sides we  have the speaker grilles on the bottom  and right here this is interesting  because they're changing up the camera  bump with a microphone right here and a  camera it's just a little different  design but you can see that the display  is not getting the same update redesign  that it did with apple's other ipads  like the ipad pro the air and the mini  those all got edge to edge displays with  even bezels all around and they got rid  of the home button but this one keeps  the home button as you can see and it  keeps the square display design which is  a bit unfortunate now here we can see  that you also have the speaker grilles  on the top with a regular power button  but  the headphone jack is gone so apple is  finally scrapping it there will be no  more ipads with the headphone jack which  makes sense because apple is going to be  selling different accessories to replace  that so like air pods or even home pod  speakers if you're at home and just to  prove to you guys that it's not going to  be that bad renders by shy lash just  created some new renders of the 2022  ipad and looking at this renders i mean  that looks awesome look at that looks  really clean you got this metal bump  design  of course you have the square display  which is unfortunate but looking at this  it still looks great look at that you  got the camera bump sticking out nice  clean design i personally think this is  totally fine for the budget ipad and i  do believe that because of usbc and the  flat sides they are going to raise the  price from the current 329 to maybe as  high as 399  or maybe 350 around there so it's gonna  be more expensive this time around but  it makes sense why now i know a lot of  people are complaining about this front  panel design with the home button the  uneven big bezels the square display but  if you think about it it actually makes  sense for apple because if they made  this edge to edge looking just like the  other ipads you wouldn't be able to tell  that this is different compared to the  ipad air other than the size difference  so you could just buy this thing pretend  you have an ipad air most people won't  know but apple wants to make sure that  if you're spending the extra money it  looks better than the budget model they  always want the budget model to look  cheap and old in comparison to their  more expensive ipads which is why i  think they went with this design and on  top of that of course this square  display is a lot cheaper to manufacture  compared to the other displays that are  edge to edge with the rounded corners  because they actually physically cut the  pixels on those displays so it is more  expensive but i am hoping for a  laminated display and then another nice  thing for apple is that because the usb  type-c port is here and it's replacing  the lightning port it is no longer going  to support the apple pencil first  generation which means that people can't  reuse their same apple pencil they have  to buy the new one so apple is making  more money with this move and now of  course we also have the m2 ipad pro  which is gonna have a pretty big  redesign now recently in june mark  german did say that it's gonna debut in  either september or october and i think  it makes total sense to be october  because apple is delaying ipad os 16  until october so that's almost  guaranteed right now it's gotta be in  october during an apple event for sure  but the big change is that we're getting  wireless charging debuting on this new  redesigned ipad pro which is a  breakthrough feature that we've never  had on an ipad because it's always been  metal and we never had anything to use  with mac safe and it's gonna eventually  reverse wireless charge your other  magsafe devices which means you could  have your ipad and then you can plop on  your airpods right on the back and max  safe charge them or in the future maybe  with the series 8 pro apple watch with  max safe you can plop that on their  charge it maybe even your iphone with a  mac save case and i do believe that the  new magic keyboard could get a  redesigned with mag safe support built  into the actual keyboard case itself so  that is going to be amazing now as far  as the performance we already know how  the m2 chip performs in the m2 macbook  air and the macbook pro and we do k